    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0501" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg429"/>

                <head>Mr. Odell to Mr. Hunter</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-21">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt this day of your letter of the 18th instant, enclosing a programme of
                    the obsequies of the late President, and inviting my attendance at the religious
                    services at the Executive mansion.</p>
                <p>Indisposition having prevented my presence at Washington on this sad occasion, I
                    take this opportunity to assure you that it was with the deepest regret that I
                    learned the great bereavement which, under such heart-rending circumstances, had
                    befallen the late President’s family and the nation. In this regret I am sure
                    his Majesty the King and his government will participate.</p>
                <p>Seldom are the living called to mourn the death of a ruler whose noble deeds had
                    gained for him such universal respect and esteem.</p>
                <p>I pray you will be pleased to express to the family of the late President the
                    sentiments which I feel on this mournful occasion.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great consideration, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. W. F. ODELL</signed>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
